  "sol": "1. Reference: CFM56-7B REV.66 15-JUL-25\n\n2. SUBTASK 72-23-00-050-061\nParagraph 3.C.3 thru 3.C.4\nRemove the AGB mount link assy.\n\n3. Machining TBR B-7\nWarning:\nTHIS OIL IS HIGHLY FLAMMABLE. TAKE PRECAUTIONS AGAINST FIRE.\n\nRemove the defective spherical bearing.\nRefer to TASK 72-09-04-300-804 (Repair 010), Paragraph 5.A\n\n4. NDT B-7\n\nDo FPI on the AGB mount link. Refer to TASK [70-32-12-230-006]\n(70-32-12, Fluorescent-Penetrant Inspection - Stationary\nPost-Emulsifiable).\n\n[  ] No defects found,   [  ] Defects found, see NDT form\n\n5. Bench Inspection B-7\n(1) The salient defects and all defects on the chamfer are not allowed.\n(2) The seizure marks, scratches or other surface defects (salient\ndefects, protrusion) more than 0.008 in. (0,20 mm) are not allowed.\nACCEPT / REJECT\n\n6. Machining TBR B-7\n\nINSTALLATION BY SHRINKING (COOLING IN LIQUID NITROGEN OR BY ANY OTHER\nPROCESS) OR THERMAL EXPANSION IS STRICTLY FORBIDDEN, BECAUSE\nCONDENSATION AFTER COOLING MAY GENERATE CORROSION WITHIN THE ASSEMBLED\nITEMS.\n\nWarning:\nMAKE SURE THAT THE TIGHTENING MENTIONED IN FIGURE 901 IS RESPECTED.\n\nInstall the new spherical bearing on the AGB mount link per ESM\n72-09-04, Repair 010. Refer to [Figure 901] for link and spherical\nbearing composition indivisible assembly.\n\n1) Apply a coat of [CP5070 Vaseline] on external surface of spherical\nbearing.\n(2) Apply a load fit on the spherical bearing into the link.\n\nNOTE:  The pressure load must be applied onto the outer ring of\nspherical bearing. Any shock is prohibited.\n\n7.  SUBTASK 72-23-00-440-068\n\nParagraph 3.L.3 thru 3.L.4\n\nInstall the AGB mount link assy.\n\nRecord torque of nuts\nActual torque: ____________lb in.\nLimit: 850-940 lb in.\nIMTE No.: ______________"
